{
  "title": "Stop test setup from implicitly upgrading the dependency lock",
  "description": "Running `make test` in a fresh worktree can invoke the \
implicit `requirements-test.lock` Makefile rule when `requirements-test.txt` \
has a newer filesystem timestamp. That rule runs `uv pip compile --upgrade`, \
so an ordinary test run can unexpectedly modify the tracked lockfile based on \
whatever package versions are current. This was observed when `make test` \
changed `charset-normalizer` from 3.4.7 to 3.4.9 without any dependency \
change.\n\
\n\
Normal setup, test, and lint targets should consume the committed lockfile \
without regenerating it. Dependency upgrades should happen only through the \
explicit `make python-test-deps-update` target. Add coverage or another \
deterministic check proving that a fresh-worktree `make test` does not dirty \
`requirements-test.lock`.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "testing",
    "tooling",
  ],
